  "content": "# Implementing a Bounded LRU Cache in Python\n\nA **Least Recently Used (LRU) cache** is a fundamental data structure that stores a fixed maximum number of key-value pairs. When the cache is full and a new item is added, the least recently accessed item is evicted. This makes it ideal for scenarios where you need fast access to recently used data but cannot store everything.\n\nPython's `collections.OrderedDict` is the perfect tool for this because it maintains insertion order and allows O(1) insertion, deletion, and lookup. Crucially, it provides `move_to_end()` which lets us reorder keys in O(1) time, making \"least recently used\" tracking trivial.\n\n## The Core Class\n\n```python\nfrom collections import OrderedDict\n\n\nclass LRUCache:\n    \"\"\"\n    A bounded LRU cache with O(1) time complexity for get and put.\n\n    - Maintains a maximum capacity `capacity`.\n    - On `get(key)`: returns value if present, marks key as most recently used.\n        Returns -1 if not present.\n    - On `put(key, value)`: inserts or updates key with value, marks key as\n        most recently used. Evicts least recently used key if capacity exceeded.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, capacity: int):\n        if capacity <= 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"Capacity must be a positive integer.\")\n        self.capacity = capacity\n        self.cache: OrderedDict[int, int] = OrderedDict()\n\n    def get(self, key: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Retrieve the value for `key`.\n        If the key exists, move it to the end (most recently used position)\n        and return its value. Otherwise, return -1.\n        \"\"\"\n        if key not in self.cache:\n            return -1\n        # Move the accessed key to the end, marking it as most recently used\n        self.cache.move_to_end(key)\n        return self.cache[key]\n\n    def put(self, key: int, value: int) -> None:\n        \"\"\"\n        Insert or update the key-value pair.\n        If the key already exists, update its value and move it to the end.\n        If the key is new and the cache is at capacity, evict the least\n        recently used item (the first item in the OrderedDict).\n        \"\"\"\n        if key in self.cache",
